course: dictionary
lesson: 13412
title: Words that show order
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe how things are organised. «Hierarchical» is one of them. Look at the clues in the sentence: levels, ranks, top and bottom, more important. Those words tell you the things are arranged in an order, one level above another.
explain: «In the castle, the king was at the top, the lords were below him, and the peasants were at the bottom.» Each group sits on a different level, and the top level has the most power. That is what hierarchical means: arranged in levels or ranks, from the top to the bottom.
explain: The word also works in science. «Scientists sort living things in a hierarchical way, from kingdom down to species.» Here the groups sit inside bigger groups, like a family tree. Always check your meaning by putting it in the sentence instead of the hard word.
fact: Hierarchical means arranged in levels or ranks, from the top to the bottom.
fact: In a hierarchical system, each level is more important or powerful than the one below it.
fact: In science, hierarchical means arranged in groups inside bigger groups, like a family tree.
fact: «Hierarchical» describes things like feudal society, schools, armies, and folders inside folders on a computer.
fact: Clue words for hierarchical include levels, ranks, top, bottom, and more powerful.
exercise: «In the army, a sergeant ranks above a private, and a captain ranks above the sergeant.» What does hierarchical mean? | Made of wood and stone | Very quiet and calm | *Arranged in levels or ranks, from top to bottom | Arranged in a circle with no leader
exercise: «Every folder on the computer sits inside another folder, which makes the system hierarchical.» What is the clue that helps you? | Everyone can use the computer | *Folders sit inside other folders | The folders are blue | The computer is turned on
exercise: Ella says hierarchical means "flat and equal". Is she right? Why or why not? | No, it means very hot | *No, it means arranged in levels, with some levels above others | Yes, every level is exactly the same | Yes, because it means round and smooth
test: «In the school, the head teacher is at the top, then the deputy heads, then the teachers.» What does this show about the school? | *The school is hierarchical, with levels from top to bottom | The school is only one room | The school has no rules at all | The school is a playground
test: Which word is closest in meaning to hierarchical in the sentence «Scientists sort living things in a hierarchical way»? | Frozen | Sleepy | *Ranked | Scattered
exam: «The king sat at the top of the feudal system, and the peasants sat at the bottom.» What does the phrase "feudal system" show about the word hierarchical? | *It is a system with levels, from the most powerful at the top to the least powerful at the bottom | It is a system where everyone has equal power | It is a type of food | It is a system with no leaders
